&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why work at FreedomCare?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are here for you and committed to providing a best-in-class employee experience. We offer competitive compensation, medical benefits, retirement plans, wellness programs, fun company events and ongoing learning opportunities to grow your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is a place where your voice matters, where we build great relationships, and your work has meaning and a tangible positive impact on others!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At FreedomCare, we celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, citizenship or immigration status, citizenship or immigration status, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;At FreedomCare, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is determined within a range. This provides our employees with the opportunity to professionally grow and develop within a role. The base pay range for this role is between $100,000 and $120,000 per year at the commencement of your first year of employment. Compensation decisions are dependent upon a variety of factors which may include, but are not limited to: skill set, years of relevant experience, education, location, and licensure/certifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Started in 2016, FreedomCare is a Healthcare company that is innovating and revolutionizing the way home care is delivered. We bring dignity and support to patients needing care in their homes and to the caregivers who care for them. We’re the largest consumer-directed home care agency in NY State and are continually expanding our areas of focus including operations in other states and tech-based innovations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pride ourselves on our values which drive the level of care that we deliver to our patients:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Here For You (An attitude of service, empathy, and availability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own It (Drive and ownership)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the Right Thing (High integrity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Positive (Great attitude and a can-do positive approach to challenges)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team and make a positive impact on the lives of others! We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Nurse Educator&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;for our Licensed HomeCare team&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is an &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;on-site&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; role that requires a regularly scheduled commute/travel to one of our locations in NYC, with a&amp;nbsp; willingness to cover additional boroughs like Manhattan and Brooklyn &amp;amp; Queens for field RN visits on occasion.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department &amp;amp; Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver training programs and support clinical staff development to ensure competency and compliance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LHCSA Nurse Educator is responsible for delivering FreedomCare&#39;s Personal Care Aide (PCA) training program, including 40-hour PCA courses, skills instruction, competency evaluation, testing, and required training documentation. The Nurse Educator also supports caregiver and clinical staff education, retraining, and competency development and performs field-based nursing work as assigned by the Director of Patient Services to support patient care, supervision, competency, and operational needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and facilitate 40-hour Personal Care Aide (PCA) training courses in accordance with NYSDOH requirements and the agency&#39;s approved curriculum, including classroom instruction, skills demonstrations, testing, and competency evaluation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for each class by ensuring required training materials, equipment, rosters, attendance records, examinations, skills checklists, and other program documentation are complete and available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain complete and audit-ready training records, including enrollment, attendance, curriculum completion, examinations, competency evaluations, remediation, completion status, and required follow-up documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide remediation, retraining, and competency refreshers when a trainee or caregiver does not demonstrate required knowledge or skills, and document all follow-up actions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Director of Patient Services, Recruitment/Certification, Compliance, and Learning &amp;amp; Development to support compliant PCA training, caregiver onboarding, and consistent education standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide orientation, education, and competency support for new field nurses and retraining or clinical refreshers for existing nursing staff as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform field-based nursing work as assigned, including patient home visits, RN assessments or reassessments as appropriate, caregiver supervisory visits, competency assessments, clinical follow-up, patient/caregiver education, and other nursing activities within RN scope of practice and agency policy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit readiness and quality improvement by maintaining accurate education records and ensuring training practices are applied consistently across LHCSA locations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure trainees meet applicable program admission and completion requirements before training completion or certification documentation is finalized.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track class attendance, completion, testing results, competency needs, outstanding requirements, and follow-up actions; promptly escalate barriers that may impact certification, patient care, or compliance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CREDENTIALS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current and unrestricted New York State Registered Professional Nurse (RN) license required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associates Degree of Nursing Required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 1 year of experience in home care services (e.g., LHCSA, CHHA, hospice) required; home care education or supervisory experience preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering healthcare training, caregiver education, competency evaluation, clinical onboarding, or adult education strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PCA training requirements, adult-learning principles, caregiver scope of practice, infection control, patient rights, and clinical documentation standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong clinical judgment and ability to teach, evaluate, and reinforce safe care within RN and PCA scope of practice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation, facilitation, written, and verbal communication skills with the ability to explain clinical and regulatory requirements clearly and professionally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage adult learners, provide constructive feedback, and adapt instruction to different learning needs while maintaining required training standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate records in Salesforce, Medflyt, training platforms, portals, and other required systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to organize multiple classes, deadlines, field requests, and follow-up needs while escalating compliance or patient-care risks promptly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to patient rights, confidentiality, HIPAA, service quality, regulatory compliance, and FreedomCare values.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK ENVIRONMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position includes office, education-site, and field-based responsibilities. The Nurse Educator is expected to travel locally as assigned to support patient visits, RN assessments or reassessments as appropriate, caregiver competency assessments, supervisory visits, clinical follow-up, audit support, patient/caregiver education, or other nursing and operational needs. Field work may vary based on training schedules and agency needs. The role requires handling confidential patient, caregiver, and employment information in accordance with HIPAA and company policy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
