&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Join our team and make a positive impact on the lives of others! &lt;strong&gt;We are looking for a Office Operations Specialist to join our LHCSA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This role is based in our FreedomCare Queens office and requires working onsite five days per week&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Office Operations Specialist is an individual contributor responsible for supporting both caregiver compliance and the day-to-day administrative operations of a LHCSA office. This role ensures caregivers meet all New York State Department of Health (NYSDOH) compliance requirements while maintaining efficient office operations that support Recruitment, Certification, and Coordination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position combines regulatory compliance responsibilities with office administration to ensure smooth onboarding, operational efficiency, and a positive caregiver experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities &amp;amp; Scope&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CHRC &amp;amp; Compliance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and monitor Criminal History Record Check (CHRC) requests in accordance with NYSDOH requirements, including initiating requests, tracking completion, and ensuring required steps are completed timely and accurately.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Live Scan submissions, fingerprint appointments, and background check results; follow up on pending, incomplete, or delayed items and escalate compliance concerns as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate caregiver compliance records and documentation to support onboarding, ongoing employment eligibility, and audit readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct routine compliance audits of caregiver files, identify missing or incomplete documentation, and partner with appropriate teams to resolve gaps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preparation for internal reviews, regulatory audits, and survey activity by organizing required records and ensuring documentation is complete and accessible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office &amp;amp; Facility Oversight&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate day-to-day office operations to ensure the LHCSA office runs smoothly, remains organized, and provides a professional environment for caregivers, candidates, employees, and visitors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ACD classroom readiness, including preparing rooms, supplies, materials, sign-in documentation, and related logistics needed to support recruitment, certification, and onboarding activity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support visitor management and front-office activity by greeting and directing visitors, assisting caregivers and candidates, and connecting individuals with the appropriate internal teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage office supplies, mail distribution, document organization, scanning, filing, and other administrative tasks needed to keep office operations accurate and efficient.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and communicate facility-related needs, coordinate follow-up with appropriate support teams, and help maintain a safe, clean, and functional office environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate caregiver support items and office hospitality needs, including preparing goodie bags for testing aides and caregivers picking up scrubs or PPE, placing lunch orders, and maintaining related office budgets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cross-functional administrative support to other LHCSA teams as needed to support caregiver onboarding and operational workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete additional projects and duties as assigned to support department priorities and evolving business needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Education and Experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of experience in healthcare administration, home care, compliance, or caregiver onboarding preferred. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous office management or office administration experience preferred. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with New York State Department of Health (NYSDOH) regulations preferred. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience processing Criminal History Record Checks (CHRC) or other background screening processes preferred but not required. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Time Tap, Salesforce, Microsoft Office, Docusign, or similar systems preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administrative support in a regulated healthcare environment. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multiple departments in a fast-paced office setting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, administrative, and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced office environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail, including the ability to maintain accurate records, audit documentation, and identify compliance gaps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer service and interpersonal skills, with the ability to support caregivers, candidates, visitors, and internal teams professionally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coordinate day-to-day office operations, maintain organized files and records, and support multiple departments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information in accordance with HIPAA and NYSDOH requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
