&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department &amp;amp; Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;FreedomCare’s Georgia operations support Structured Family Caregiving (SFC), a Medicaid home and community-based service option that helps eligible individuals receive daily care from a qualified live-in family caregiver, with coaching and oversight to support safe care at home.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The Team Lead is responsible for the day-to-day management, coaching, and development of a team of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Homecare Sales Specialists. This team’s goal is to educate prospective patients and caregivers, assessing eligibility, and supporting enrollment progression through Service Record creation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; This role ensures team members have the guidance, workflow clarity, performance support, and accountability needed to deliver accurate, timely, compliant, and customer-focused service to prospective patients.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:25,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:271,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:10}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The Team Lead of HomeCare Sales is critical in translating operational priorities into daily execution by monitoring queues, reviewing performance data, managing attendance and schedule adherence, supporting quality standards, and resolving escalations. This role requires strong people leadership, operational discipline, clear communication, data-informed coaching, and a commitment to developing high-performing teams while maintaining a compassionate, patient-first approach.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:25,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:280,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:271,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:10}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Every Day You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Directly supervise a team of Specialists, executing daily operational priorities, participating in coaching, attendance management, performance management, development planning, and recognition activities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Serve as the primary point of contact for team member questions, concerns, and escalated issues, ensuring timely resolution and appropriate escalation when needed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Manage and monitor attendance, punctuality, and schedule adherence to ensure adequate coverage, operational efficiency, and achievement of service-level goals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Monitor daily workflows, workload distribution, call queue activity, and productivity to ensure team members meet performance expectations, customer service standards, policies, procedures, and compliance guidelines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Drive performance against established KPIs, including quality scores, conversion rates, productivity metrics, schedule adherence, attendance, customer satisfaction measures, and other operational indicators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Deliver effective coaching and development through regular performance discussions, data-driven feedback, real-time coaching, and structured follow-up plans focused on productivity, efficiency, quality, compliance, and customer service excellence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Conduct reviews of service records, documentation, phone calls, and operational data to ensure accuracy, quality, compliance, and adherence to organizational standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Use performance data, quality findings, customer feedback, and operational insights to develop action plans that support continuous improvement and team objective achievement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Ensure team members consistently adhere to company policies, standard operating procedures, HIPAA requirements, privacy standards, and other applicable regulatory guidelines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Identify system, workflow, or process improvement opportunities that enhance team performance, quality, efficiency, compliance, and customer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Communicate organizational updates, process changes, performance expectations, and training initiatives from leadership and cross-functional teams to direct reports, ensuring understanding and consistent execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Interview, onboard, train, and develop Specialists while fostering a culture of accountability, engagement, continuous learning, and high performance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt; Support relationships with external partners and organizations as needed to resolve operational issues and support department objectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal Candidate Will Possess:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:540,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required, bachelor’s degree preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:540,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;2&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Experience managing, supervising, or informally leading a group or team of employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence, motivate, and support employees while fostering accountability and high performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, critical-thinking, and time-management skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze data, identify performance trends, and implement improvement strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to clearly explain expectations, feedback, process changes, and next steps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective conflict resolution, decision-making, and problem-solving abilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to quality, compliance, and accurate documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of compliance requirements, privacy standards, and organizational policies and procedures, with the ability to reinforce and monitor adherence across the team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment while maintaining consistency, follow-through, and operational discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why work at FreedomCare?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are here for you and committed to providing a best-in-class employee experience.&amp;nbsp; We offer competitive compensation, medical benefits, retirement plans, wellness programs, fun company events and ongoing learning opportunities to grow your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is a place where your voice matters, where we build great relationships, and your work has meaning and a tangible positive impact on others!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At FreedomCare, we celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, citizenship or immigration status, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;At FreedomCare, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is determined within a range. This provides our employees with the opportunity to professionally grow and develop within a role. The base pay range for this role is between $23.00 and $26.00 an hour at the commencement of your first year of employment. Compensation decisions are dependent upon a variety of factors which may include, but are not limited to: skill set, years of relevant experience, education, location, and licensure/certifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$23&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$26 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FreedomCare is a healthcare company that has been dedicated to revolutionizing the home care industry since 2016. We support our patients by ensuring they have the power to choose a caregiver who will care for them in the comfort of their own homes. Our mission spans coast to coast, supporting patients across the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pride ourselves on our values which drive the level of care that we deliver to our patients:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Here For You (An attitude of service, empathy, and availability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own It (Drive and ownership)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the Right Thing (High integrity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Positive (Great attitude and a can-do positive approach to challenges)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team and make a positive impact on the lives of others! We are looking for a Team Lead of Michigan to support our growing and emerging Michigan team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position with travel into our main office located in Southfield, Michigan. This role will require working from our FreedomCare MI office 3x a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Department &amp;amp; Position Overview:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a patient and caregiver focused leadership role providing a seamless customer service experience by effectively leading a team of empathetic and solutions-driven team members within our growing Michigan operations. The Team Lead will mentor and advise team members to provide exceptional service to patients and caregivers while supporting the day-to-day operational needs of the Michigan market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As FreedomCare continues to grow and develop its presence in Michigan, this role will support evolving operational needs across the patient and caregiver journey, including intake, engagement, enrollment, service readiness, and other operational functions necessary to support the Michigan market. The Team Lead will work closely with Michigan leadership to support effective workflows, team performance, quality, compliance, and continuous improvement as the state operation continues to expand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every Day You Will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the direct point-of-contact for team member inquiries or concerns; respond to and resolve escalated or complex issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the performance of team members through active motivation, assessing performance, consistent communication, coaching, and effective feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor daily Michigan workflows to ensure team members are meeting performance goals, following standard policies and procedures, and remaining within applicable compliance guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support operational activities associated with the MDHHS Adult Home Help Program and other applicable Michigan programs, service models, and operational needs as the market evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the patient and caregiver journey from initial engagement through enrollment and service readiness, helping to identity and resolve barriers that may delay progression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor process improvement by identifying system or workflow areas of opportunity and supporting the development of scalable solutions for the growing Michigan market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development, implementation, and refinement of Michigan-specific workflows and operational processes as the state continues to grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for disseminating information and training from senior management and other departments to direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor operational performance, workflow trends, capacity, and team readiness and escalate identified risks or barriers to Michigan leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support Michigan operational needs and the successful progression of patients and caregivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview candidates, train employees, and provide continued training, coaching, and development to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support additional operational responsibilities as needed based on the evolving needs and growth of FreedomCare&#39;s&lt;br&gt;Michigan market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal Candidate Will Possess:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing/supervising a group or team of employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional experience leading, mentoring, coaching, and developing employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in FreedomCare processes and systems, with the ability to learn and support evolving&lt;br&gt;Michigan-specific workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead effectively within a growing and evolving operation where processes, priorities, and responsibilities may continue to develop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with a drive to meet and exceed operational targets and performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to motivate a team to meet and/or exceed operational targets and metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, critical thinking, problem-solving, and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, able to work independently, and able to make informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify operational barriers and work collaboratively to develop effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability and willingness to support expanding responsibilities as Michigan operations continue to grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives mission, core values, and vision&lt;br&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Business Administration or Healthcare Administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a home care agency, hospital, healthcare organization, or healthcare operations environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Medicaid, community-based services, or Michigan healthcare programs preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience managing 5+ employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a growing, emerging, or rapidly evolving operation is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish bilingual is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
